{"abstract":"Relation Extraction (RE) is at the core of many Natural Language Understanding tasks, including knowledge-base population and Question Answering. However, any Natural Language Processing system is exposed to biases, and the analysis of these has not received much attention in RE. We propose a new method for inspecting bias in the RE pipeline, which is completely transparent in terms of interpretability. Specifically, in this work we analyze biases related to gender and place of birth. Our methodology includes (i) obtaining semantic triplets (subject, object, semantic relation) involving ‘person’ entities from RE resources, (ii) collecting meta-information (‘gender’ and ‘place of birth’) using Entity Linking technologies, and then (iii) analyze the distribution of triplets across different groups (e.g., men versus women). We investigate bias at two levels: In the training data of three commonly used RE datasets (SREDFM, CrossRE, NYT), and in the predictions of a state-of-the-art RE approach (ReLiK). To enable cross-dataset analysis, we introduce a taxonomy of relation types mapping the label sets of different RE datasets to a unified label space. Our findings reveal that bias is a compounded issue affecting underrepresented groups within data and predictions for RE.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Stranisci, Marco Antonio","Huguet Cabot, Pere-Lluís","Bassignana, Elisa","Navigli, Roberto"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759395"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Sapienza University of Rome","University of Turin"],"keyword":["Bias analysis","Gender bias","Place of Birth","Relation Extraction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dissecting biases in relation extraction a cross dataset analysis on people s gender and origin","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.gebnlp-1.12.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759395","identifier":[{"id":"85204359185","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-3a4d3f5a-5532-4f39-9b18-8888edd73fe8"],"keyword":["Bias Analysis","Cross-dataset Evaluation","Gender Bias","Place of Birth","Relation Extraction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A9418B5EEB829547AD93D45067067AC1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.gebnlp-1.12/","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.gebnlp-1.12.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of turin","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Turin","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"sapienza university of rome","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Sapienza University of Rome","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco Antonio","key":"straniscipau","last":"Stranisci","name":"Stranisci, Marco Antonio","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pere-Lluís","key":"huguetcabotpau","last":"Huguet Cabot","name":"Huguet Cabot, Pere-Lluís","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisa","key":"bassignanapau","last":"Bassignana","locid":"c6b67626-5ff8-4730-93a6-70ee08f6013e","name":"Bassignana, Elisa","orcid":"0009-0003-8374-7571","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Roberto","key":"naviglipau","last":"Navigli","name":"Navigli, Roberto","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"190-202","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 5th Workshop on Gender Bias in Natural Language Processing (GeBNLP)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3a4d3f5a-5532-4f39-9b18-8888edd73fe8"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Dissecting Biases in Relation Extraction: A Cross-Dataset Analysis on People’s Gender and Origin","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759395","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
